TTYCHATTER(1)              User Commands              TTYCHATTER(1)

NAME
    ttychatter - traditional command-line OpenRouter chat client

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter [options] input.txt output.log
    ttychatter --interactive [output.log]
    ttychatter --demo --interactive [output.log]
    ttychatter --set-api-key [--gpg]
    ttychatter --forget-api-key
    ttychatter --models [--demo] [--search TEXT] [--model-type TYPE]
               [--sort ORDER] [--favorites-only]
    ttychatter --update-models [--demo]
    ttychatter --test-model MODEL [--demo]
    ttychatter --favorites
    ttychatter --favorite-model MODEL
    ttychatter --unfavorite-model MODEL
    ttychatter --config
    ttychatter --set KEY=VALUE
    ttychatter --unset KEY
    ttychatter --doctor
    ttychatter --version
    ttychatter --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter is the C command-line client in the ttychatter family.

    It is intentionally not the ncurses interface.  The primary workflow is a
    traditional Unix file-in/file-out model: the user prepares an input file,
    runs ttychatter, and ttychatter appends the AI response to an output file.

        ttychatter input.txt output.log

    The output file is also the session state.  Reusing the same output file
    resumes the conversation because ttychatter reads recent turns from that
    file and sends them as context.

    ttychatter also provides an optional line-oriented interactive mode with
    colon commands.  This exists to preserve feature parity with the Bash
    clients without turning the C client into an ncurses program.

BASIC FILE WORKFLOW
    Create an input prompt:

        cat > input.txt
        Explain what DNS caching means.
        ^D

    Send it and append the response to a session file:

        ttychatter input.txt session.log

    Continue the same session:

        vi followup.txt
        ttychatter followup.txt session.log

INTERACTIVE MODE
    Start an interactive line-oriented session:

        ttychatter --interactive session.log

    Or use demo mode without network access:

        ttychatter --demo --interactive demo.log

    In interactive mode, normal lines are sent to the AI model.  Lines that
    begin with ':' are local ttychatter commands and are not sent to the model.

    Common runtime commands:

        :help
        :models
        :routers
        :update-models
        :test-model MODEL
        :model MODEL
        :model-save MODEL
        :favorites
        :favorite MODEL
        :unfavorite MODEL
        :config
        :set KEY VALUE
        :unset KEY
        :set-api-key
        :set-api-key gpg
        :forget-api-key
        :memory
        :attach FILE
        :attachments
        :clear-attachments
        :editor
        :search TEXT
        :search-all TEXT
        :credits
        :doctor
        :quit

    To send a literal message beginning with ':' prefix it with a backslash:

        \:this line is sent to the model

DEMO MODE
    Demo mode uses local model rows and local canned responses.  It does not
    require an OpenRouter API key and does not contact OpenRouter.

        ttychatter --demo --models
        ttychatter --demo --test-model demo/large-context
        ttychatter --demo input.txt session.log
        ttychatter --demo --interactive session.log

API KEY SETUP
    Store the OpenRouter API key encrypted with GPG:

        ttychatter --set-api-key --gpg

    Store the OpenRouter API key in plaintext config:

        ttychatter --set-api-key

    Plaintext storage is convenient but less safe.  Encrypted GPG storage uses
    the external gpg command and stores the key at API_KEY_GPG_FILE.

    Environment variables are also supported:

        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        TTYCHATTER_API_KEY

CONFIGURATION
    Default config file:

        ~/.config/ttychatter/config

    Inspect active configuration:

        ttychatter --config

    Set or unset values:

        ttychatter --set CONTEXT_TURNS=20
        ttychatter --unset MODEL

    Common keys:

        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
            Plaintext API key. Environment variables override this.

        API_KEY_GPG_FILE
            Path to encrypted API key file.
            Default: ~/.config/ttychatter/api-key.gpg

        MODEL
            OpenRouter model/router.
            Default: openrouter/auto

        CONTEXT_TURNS
            Recent user/assistant turns read from the output log and sent as
            conversation context.
            Default: 12

        MODEL_CACHE_FILE
            OpenRouter model catalog cache.
            Default: ~/.cache/ttychatter/models.json

        MODEL_FAVORITES_FILE
            Newline-delimited model favorites file.

        MODEL_SORT_ORDER
            Default sort order for model listing.
            Values: name, context, tokens, type, favorites

        SESSION_DIR
            Default session directory for helper commands and session search.

        ATTACHMENT_DIR
            Directory for extracted code-block attachments.

        CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES
            Minimum line count before a returned fenced code block is saved as
            an attachment rather than left inline.
            Default: 5

        MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES
            Maximum local attachment size for inline sending.
            Default: 1048576

        CONFIRM_LIVE_SEND
            If true, ask before making a real OpenRouter chat-completions
            request. The --yes option bypasses this confirmation.

        STARTUP_NOTICE
            If true, a new output/session file begins with a human-readable
            Project Lead notice block. That block is not sent as provider
            context.

        LOOPBACK
            If true, print AI output to stdout in addition to appending it to
            the session log.

MODEL CATALOG
    Refresh the OpenRouter model cache:

        ttychatter --update-models

    List cached models:

        ttychatter --models

    Search cached models:

        ttychatter --models --search llama

    Show routers, fixed models, free models, or favorites:

        ttychatter --models --model-type routers
        ttychatter --models --model-type fixed
        ttychatter --models --model-type free
        ttychatter --models --favorites-only

    Sort the model list:

        ttychatter --models --sort name
        ttychatter --models --sort context
        ttychatter --models --sort type
        ttychatter --models --sort favorites

MODEL FAVORITES
    Add, remove, and list bookmarked models:

        ttychatter --favorite-model openrouter/auto
        ttychatter --unfavorite-model openrouter/auto
        ttychatter --favorites

ATTACHMENTS
    Attach files with repeated -a options:

        ttychatter -a notes.txt -a image.png input.txt session.log

    Text files are inserted into the text prompt. Image files are sent as
    OpenRouter chat content parts when the chosen model supports image input.
    Other binary files are listed in the prompt but not fully embedded.

CODE BLOCK EXTRACTION
    Long fenced code blocks in AI responses are saved under ATTACHMENT_DIR.
    Short fenced blocks remain inline.  CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES controls the
    threshold.

LOOPBACK
    Print the clean AI response to stdout while still appending to the session
    log:

        ttychatter --loopback input.txt session.log | tee latest.txt

    Mirror the clean AI response to a file:

        ttychatter --loopback-file latest.txt input.txt session.log

FILES
    ~/.config/ttychatter/config
        Configuration file.

    ~/.config/ttychatter/api-key.gpg
        Default encrypted API-key file.

    ~/.cache/ttychatter/models.json
        Default model catalog cache.

    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/sessions/
        Default session directory used by helper commands.

    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/attachments/
        Default extracted attachment directory.

LIMITATIONS
    - This is not an ncurses program.
    - Interactive mode is a line-oriented REPL, not a full-screen interface.
    - Binary/media attachment support depends on provider and model support.
    - Encrypted API-key storage depends on the external gpg program.

VERSION
    ttychatter 0.4.0-c-cli

AUTHOR
    Part of the ttychatter terminal chat client project.
